{"name":"Bara Red","hex":"#e9546b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bara","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A genre of homoerotic media, usually also pornographic, typically created by gay men and targeted at gay men in Japan.","A genre of homoerotic or pornographic media of a similar style and aesthetic, regardless of the creator's gender or ethnicity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or related to media in the bara genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bara"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bara (genre)","blocks":[{"text":"Bara  is a colloquialism for a genre of Japanese art and media known within Japan as gay manga (ゲイ漫画) or gei komi . The genre focuses on male same-sex love, as created primarily by gay men for a gay male audience. Bara can vary in visual style and plot but typically features masculine men with varying degrees of muscle, body fat, and body hair, akin to bear or bodybuilding culture. While bara is typically pornographic, the genre has also depicted romantic and autobiographical subject material, as it acknowledges the varied reactions to homosexuality in modern Japan."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bara_(genre)","wikidata":"Q18655723"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg/500px-Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg/1280px-Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg/500px-Rosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The term bara translates literally to \"rose\" in Japanese, and has historically been used as a pejorative for gay men roughly equivalent to the English language term \"pansy\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_Red_Chateau01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Saginoike_Heikur%C5%8D_Masatora_by_Kuniyoshi.jpg/330px-Saginoike_Heikur%C5%8D_Masatora_by_Kuniyoshi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Saginoike_Heikur%C5%8D_Masatora_by_Kuniyoshi.jpg/330px-Saginoike_Heikur%C5%8D_Masatora_by_Kuniyoshi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A musha-e print by Utagawa Kuniyoshi (c. 1834)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASagin